course: dictionary
lesson: 3906
title: Frighten and its friends
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a feeling, and some name what causes it. To frighten means to make someone feel scared. Look at the words around it to see who feels scared and why. «A puffed-up tail and an arched back mean a cat is frightened.» The cat's body shows it is scared, so frightened means feeling scared.
explain: Frighten also has a phrase: to frighten away or off means to scare an animal or person so they go away. If shouting makes birds fly off, the birds have been frightened away. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: Notice the forms: frighten, frightens, frightened and frightening. «Frightened» describes how a person or animal feels. «Frightening» describes the thing that causes the fear, like a frightening storm. Storms and ghosts often frighten characters in stories.
fact: Frighten means to make someone feel scared.
fact: «Frightened» means feeling scared; «frightening» means something that causes fear.
fact: To frighten away or off means to scare an animal or person so they go away.
fact: A frightened animal may bite or run, so give it space.
fact: Being frightened is normal, and courage means doing the right thing while still feeling afraid.
exercise: «A puffed-up tail and an arched back mean a cat is frightened.» What does frightened mean here? | *Feeling scared | Cold | Sleepy | Proud
exercise: Shouting in the park made the ducks fly off. Which phrase means the same as frighten off? | Call over | Wait for | *Scare away | Feed up
exercise: Which word describes a storm that makes people feel scared? | hungry | ancient | *frightening | frightened
test: «In the cold, dark, narrow passage he lags behind, gets frightened, rushes forward and knocks Rat into Mole.» What does frightened show about him? | Proud | *Scared | Sleepy | Cold
test: At tea Grandad says being frightened means you're a coward. What is the best reply? | Being frightened means you are weak | Only brave people feel afraid | *Being frightened does not make someone a coward; courage means doing the right thing while feeling afraid | Cowards never feel scared
exam: Which phrase means to scare an animal so it goes away? | Hide away | *Frighten off | Stay still | Call home
